<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia63c63fad496d8a97bb613c44a760950e513f271" commit="74f891b65f80778cc292a6c79913cf1a9194ac2d" commit_message="make.conf.sdk-chromeos: new fragment to hold internal SDK settings  The chromeos-overlay/make.conf file currently impacts both boards and the sdk.  This hasn't been a problem previously as we had very little in there, but as we try to add more customizations for boards, we're making it problematic for the sdk.  Start a new file just for the sdk so we avoid such problems.  BUG=chromium:440498 TEST=updating an sdk has same settings, as does creating a new sdk  Change-Id: Ia63c63fad496d8a97bb613c44a760950e513f271 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/391592 Commit-Ready: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrew de los Reyes &lt;adlr@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="391592" owner_email="vapier@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/92/391592/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2f851acd24c8d1d2248ac8fde1bfdacb24006d01" commit="17497761a488ed069f6b3ea0a0ac6d05f773ee1f" commit_message="sdk: switch make.conf fragments for internal sdk builds  Use the new dedicated make.conf fragment for internal sdk builds rather than the one shared between boards and the sdk.  BUG=chromium:440498 TEST=updating an sdk has same settings, as does creating a new sdk CQ-DEPEND=CL:391592  Change-Id: I2f851acd24c8d1d2248ac8fde1bfdacb24006d01 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/392166 Commit-Ready: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrew de los Reyes &lt;adlr@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="392166" owner_email="vapier@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/crosutils" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/crosutils" ref="refs/changes/66/392166/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6a169f5d4444e97ee36b25f5ce1b3b2138e36a5a" commit="a794060101841cd9d5e0c7a97cd3d423454c23a9" commit_message="dome: front-end: prepend slashes before all URLs  The URL is suppose to contain a slash to indicate that it starts from the root. Otherwise, once we introduce the routing logic, it will surely be broken.  BUG=None TEST=Manually tested  Change-Id: I6a169f5d4444e97ee36b25f5ce1b3b2138e36a5a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/393549 Commit-Ready: Mao Huang &lt;littlecvr@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mao Huang &lt;littlecvr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="393549" owner_email="littlecvr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/49/393549/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4c1ca01101efdc30081afc94312399124fa8e358" commit="050ac8ea8a2c1a69605777c63dd12bc8b081fc9d" commit_message="login: Add free-disk-size check on StartArcInstance().  This CL is the session_manager side change for moving free disk size check from Chrome. The corresponding check is https://cs.chromium.org/chromium/src/components/arc/arc_bridge_bootstrap.cc?q=arc_bridge_bootstrap.cc&amp;sq=package:chromium&amp;dr&amp;l=313  BUG=chromium:628124, chromium:633258, b:30498714 TEST=Ran on test device. Ran unittests.  Change-Id: I4c1ca01101efdc30081afc94312399124fa8e358 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/393628 Commit-Ready: Hidehiko Abe &lt;hidehiko@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hidehiko Abe &lt;hidehiko@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hidehiko Abe &lt;hidehiko@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="393628" owner_email="hidehiko@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/28/393628/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-5.39" change_id="I46d92b90763af3260355ba237165b6be3ad29e94" commit="3d374b8d0a52d77d78b24c7bec79a50c60f221c6" commit_message="CHROMIUM: supports a new dbus method ResetAdvertising  This patch supports a new dbus method ResetAdvertising which removes all existing advertisements and resets the advertising intervals to default. Note that advertising would be disabled when the last advertisement is removed.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:390172 BUG=chromium:602461 TEST=Perform the following steps on a DUT. On a terminal, use btmon to monitor the logs. $ btmon  On another terminal, execute the following steps: 1. Copy example-advertisement to the DUT, and    run the command on the DUT.    $ ./example-advertisement &amp;  2. Copy example-advertising-intervals to the DUT and    run the command on the DUT.    $ ./example-advertising-intervals --set 200 200  3. On another machine, use hcitool to observe advertising packets of the DUT.    $ sudo hcitool lescan  4. Reset advertising on the DUT.    $ ./example-advertising-intervals --reset    Observe that advertisements are removed in the btmon log and    advertising is disabled.  Change-Id: I46d92b90763af3260355ba237165b6be3ad29e94 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/390191 Commit-Ready: Miao-chen Chou &lt;mcchou@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shyh-In Hwang &lt;josephsih@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Miao-chen Chou &lt;mcchou@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Rahul Chaturvedi &lt;rkc@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Miao-chen Chou &lt;mcchou@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="390191" owner_email="josephsih@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/bluez" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/bluez" ref="refs/changes/91/390191/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2217f33915ab8b4d872a9498def6d6862f4b1913" commit="f9bdb097c6cf17b4c3dc2789a704665d43979b2f" commit_message="tpm: do not try running endorsement commands before nvram is available  Recent tpm2 repository changes introduced more strict checks of the NV RAM operations' return status. The problem is that in case TPM is not manufactured tpm_endorse() is invoked before nvram is declared available, and this causes endorsement operation failure.  Make sure NVRAM initialization is complete before endorsement is attempted.  BRANCH=none BUG=none TEST=tpm manufacturing now succeeds again.  Change-Id: I2217f33915ab8b4d872a9498def6d6862f4b1913 Signed-off-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/394129 Tested-by: Marius Schilder &lt;mschilder@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Marius Schilder &lt;mschilder@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="394129" owner_email="vbendeb@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/29/394129/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3d649d579970845c59a4f8072d2e60d3b0be5abe" commit="3a0031d8719002771317278a13d9c8fb096dcb89" commit_message="[autotest] Add support for suite scheduler to schedule suites to run on testbed  This change enables suite scheduler to parse the dut count from boards setting, and use that to update the build name (append #[dut_count]) used in creating suite job.  BUG=b:31889351 TEST=local run suite_scheduler, unittest /usr/local/autotest/site_utils/suite_scheduler/suite_scheduler.py \   -d /usr/local/autotest/logs -f /usr/local/autotest/test_ss.ini  \   -e nightly  -i git_mnc-release/shamu-us